t_vs_hist":-0.0012571177906761655,"_gp_mult_vs_hist":false,"_score_mult_vs_hist":66.8,"_gate_fcf_yield":0.045706702665577484,"_gp_fcf_yield":false,"_score_fcf_yield":22.0,"_gate_int_coverage":39.484848484848484,"_gp_int_coverage":true,"_score_int_coverage":100.0,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":1.4686178861788617,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":56.3,"_gate_accruals":-0.015008972755451629,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":24.2,"_gate_rev_volatility":41.847400711874876,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":0.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.05795282475637428,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":27.6,"_gate_piotroski":7,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":77.8,"_gate_spread":0.01778145395932404,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":8.9,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.4158351296837686,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":30.7,"_gate_incr_roic":0.4395985361845302,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.09359445936152874,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":64.5,"_gate_pool_share":0.045557020468144804,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":58.2,"_gate_rev_durability":0.02072920850756188,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":35.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.18827884450636834,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.006841355527302945,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":56.8,"_gate_fund_growth":0.07516444711009045,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":75.2,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.013871452785715957,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":26.5,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0009366759376190359,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":51.2,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.007484087570819053,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":87.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.01101,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.364,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":36.4,"pf":[],"description_full":"Mueller Water Products, Inc. manufactures and markets products and services for the transmission, distribution, and measurement of water used by municipalities, and the residential and non-residential construction industries in the United States, Canada, and internationally. It operates in two segments, Water Flow Solutions and Water Management Solutions. The Water Flow Solutions segment provides valves for water systems, such as iron gate, butterfly, tapping, check, knife, plug, and ball valves, which are used to control distribution and transmission of potable water and non-potable water, as well as in water transmission or distribution, water treatment facilities, or industrial applications. It also offers service brass products. The Water Management Solutions segment offers dry-barrel and wet-barrel fire hydrants for water infrastructure development; fire protection systems, and water infrastructure repair and replacement projects; pipe repair products, such as couplings, grips, and clamps used to repair leaks; residential, fire protection, and commercial water metering products and systems; water leak detection and pipe condition assessment products and services; machines and tools for tapping, drilling, extracting, installing, and stopping-off; gas valve products for use in gas distribution systems; and intelligent water solutions, including pressure control valves, advanced pressure management, network analytics, event management, and date logging. It sells its products under the Canada Valve, Centurion, Ez-Max, Hydro Gate, Hydro-Guard, HYMAX, HYMAX VERSA, Jones, Krausz, Milliken, Mueller Systems, Mueller, Pratt, Pratt Industrial, Repamax, Repaflex, Singer, Echologics, Echoshore, ePulse, Hersey, LeakFinderRT, Sentryx, and U.S. Pipe Valve and Hydrant brands. Mueller Water Products, Inc. was founded in 1857 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Paul  McAndrew | President, CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["MUELLER WATER PRODUCTS is a mid-cap industrials business with a $3.8B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 32%.","The business throws off $172M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 12 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.14\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 39\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.4%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.10891791887478067},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2509404.93},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Valued at a 27% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","19 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Did Sales Guidance Just Shift Mueller Water Products (MWA) Investment Narrative?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-mwa/mueller-water-products/news/did-sales-guidance-just-shift-mueller-water-products-mwa-inv","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794619892.16,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (MWA) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/43/The_Technical_Signals_Behind_MWA_That_Institutions_Follow_111226031401_1794514441.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794514441.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Mueller Water Products (MWA) Tests Its Valuation On Earnings Beat And Metering Exit","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stoc